WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.700
Alaska in 1964 involved subduction-related thrusting and major tsunami damage.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.180
San Francisco in 1906 involved the San Andreas strike-slip system, with

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.640
shaking and extensive fires. The 1994 Northridge event involved a buried

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.500
thrust fault. A damaging fault can remain hidden below the surface;

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.180
absence of an obvious exposed trace is not proof of safety.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.720
The 1959 Hebgen Lake event near Yellowstone involved normal faulting.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.280
The Madison Canyon landslide buried part of the valley and formed

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.920
Earthquake Lake; do not relabel the fault mechanism as a volcanic

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:34.220
eruption.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.940
The 1985 Mexico earthquake originated in a coastal subduction setting.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.940
Mexico City suffered severe damage far from the source because lake

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.040
sediments and basin geometry amplified the shaking.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:50.360
The event source and the damaged city are different locations.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.520
A city need not sit directly on the ruptured plate boundary

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.320
to experience destructive shaking. San Francisco’s fires and Mexico City’s sediment

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.500
response illustrate different pathways from one earthquake to widespread destruction.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.440
Magnitude alone does not determine the final losses.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:12.000
The 1811–1812 New Madrid sequence reactivated an ancient zone of weakness

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.800
within North America. Modern stress can act on old structures far

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.120
from a present plate boundary.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.800
Charleston experienced a damaging earthquake in 1886.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:24.800
The supplied chapter treats its exact tectonic cause as debated;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.940
do not turn that uncertainty into a settled fault mechanism.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:32.140
Use the historical examples to connect setting, ground conditions, and damage.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:36.400
Death tolls, estimated magnitudes, and rupture lengths differ among records;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.680
the lab prioritizes the supported mechanisms over disputed exact totals.
